 "endCard": 65.1667,
 "end": {
  "title": "Next drop: spaghetti never breaks in *two*",
  "follow": "Follow Reality Rulebook",
  "foot": "Cross and Wheatland, Am. J. Phys. 80, 1051 (2012): typical slinky collapse time about 0.3 s."
 },
 "voice": [
  {
   "id": "vo01",
   "t": 0.1,
   "dur": 2.454,
   "file": "vo/01.wav",
   "text": "Does a slinky's bottom fall? Not yet."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo02",
   "t": 3.3333333333333335,
   "dur": 7.542,
   "file": "vo/02.wav",
   "text": "Held by the top, a slinky hangs long and still. Let go. The top drops… and the bottom doesn't move at all."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo03",
   "t": 11.566666666666666,
   "dur": 7.209,
   "file": "vo/03.wav",
   "text": "Slowed down, the top coils pile up from above, while the bottom floats there. For about three tenths of a second."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo04",
   "t": 19.4,
   "dur": 13.488,
   "file": "vo/04.wav",
   "text": "Why doesn't it fall? Nothing down there has been told. The pull of the spring doesn't jump to the other end; it travels down the coils, like a wave. Until the news arrives, the bottom has no reason to move."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo05",
   "t": 35.06666666666667,
   "dur": 8.757,
   "file": "vo/05.wav",
   "text": "And the middle? It falls the whole time, like a dropped ball. The top rushes down, the bottom waits, and the average is a plain fall."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo06",
   "t": 47.13333333333333,
   "dur": 8.286,
   "file": "vo/06.wav",
   "text": "Measure it: the bottom's ghosts stack in one place for three tenths of a second. Then the top arrives, and they all go together."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo07",
   "t": 56.266666666666666,
   "dur": 3.401,
   "file": "vo/07.wav",
   "text": "Even through a spring, news travels at a limited speed."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo08",
   "t": 60.56666666666667,
   "dur": 4.486,
   "file": "vo/08.wav",
   "text": "Next: dry spaghetti, bent until it snaps. It never breaks in two."
  }
 ]
}